sequenceDiagram
  actor U as User
  participant F as :Frontend
  participant G as :Gems
  participant P as :Google Places API
  participant DB as :Database

  U->>F: tap "Add gem"
  F->>F: get the device's location (asks for permission if needed)
  alt location permission denied
    F-->>U: dialog: location is needed to add a gem
  else location available
    U->>F: select type filters T (optional)
    F->>+G: GET /place/nearby (location, types T)
    G->>+P: nearby search, 200 m around the user, types T
    P-->>-G: places, unknown type, or error
    opt places found
      G->>+DB: which of these places are already gems (they are left out)
      DB-->>-G: names of existing gems, or an error
    end
    G-->>-F: 200 [places that are not gems yet, nearest first], 400 "Invalid place type.", 502 "Google Places unavailable.", or 500 "Nearby search failed."
    alt 200 with places
      F-->>U: list of nearby places that can be added
      U->>F: pick place places/{id}
      Note over U,F: continues in the second diagram with places/{id}
    else 200 with no places
      F-->>U: "No places found within 200 m"
    else 400 unknown type
      F-->>U: "Unknown filter, try another"
    else 502 Google unavailable
      F-->>U: "Can't reach Google right now, try again later"
    else 500 database error
      F-->>U: "Couldn't load nearby places, try again"
    end
  end
  Note over U,DB: If the server can't be reached, the Frontend shows "No connection, try again"
